{"lines":[{"y":0.046460177234962319,"w":0.05555555343627927,"c":1,"x":0.84482758717074924,"h":0.013274336283185861,"t":"Test 1"},{"c":1,"y":0.094476744324101691,"t":"renewable sources, such as the sun and wind, without causing pollution. Today I'll outline marine","x":0.088122596787650873,"h":0.013081395068451962,"w":0.72222223917643225},{"w":0.71264368693033853,"c":1,"t":"renewable energy - also called ocean energy - which harnesses the movement of the oceans.","x":0.08812260087789392,"y":0.11046511641701473,"h":0.01311263302635457},{"h":0.015010526297818849,"c":1,"t":"Marine renewable energy can be divided into three main categories: wave energy, tidal","y":0.13369451642456665,"w":0.668670654296875,"x":0.089990394890183248},{"x":0.090038307326568368,"w":0.67049809773763025,"h":0.01327433628318575,"t":"energy and ocean thermal energy conversion, and I'll say a few words about each one.","c":1,"y":0.15107458922259931},{"t":"First, wave energy. Numerous devices have been invented to harvest wave energy, with names","y":0.17439691067682661,"w":0.71656489054361971,"h":0.015884190835482537,"c":1,"x":0.089982272058793555},{"h":0.014549583912498498,"c":1,"w":0.68199234008789067,"x":0.086206894998312952,"y":0.19184576503472739,"t":"such as Wave Dragon, the Penguin and Mighty Whale, and research is going on to try and"},{"t":"come up with a really efficient method. This form of energy has plenty of potential, as the source","h":0.013081395068451962,"c":1,"y":0.20784883734676973,"w":0.72030649820963544,"x":0.090038321660667581},{"c":1,"w":0.71072794596354172,"h":0.013274336283185861,"t":"is constant, and there's no danger of waves coming to a standstill. Electricity can be generated","x":0.088122616923448138,"y":0.22376738323921919},{"t":"Q32","h":0.013081395068451962,"y":0.22383720940163887,"c":1,"x":0.81992337126539672,"w":0.036398468017578289},{"w":0.68390803019205737,"t":"using onshore systems, using a reservoir, or offshore systems. But the problem with ocean","h":0.014599197281597531,"y":0.23982558128022846,"x":0.086206904311665375,"c":1},{"c":1,"x":0.086206902883663658,"y":0.25568900154219332,"t":"waves is that they're erratic, with the wind making them travel in every direction. This adds to","w":0.6992337036132813,"h":0.014659835776848595},{"h":0.013081395068452073,"c":1,"t":"Q33","y":0.25581395358768533,"w":0.036398468017578289,"x":0.81992337126539672},{"y":0.2718023254670523,"t":"the difficulty of creating efficient technology: ideally all the waves would travel smoothly and","h":0.014544071650836488,"x":0.086206897617404743,"w":0.68773946126302088,"c":1},{"w":0.71839080810546874,"t":"regularly along the same straight line. Another drawback is that sand and other sediment on the","x":0.088122603479970113,"y":0.28779069781200539,"c":1,"h":0.013094258217986376},{"t":"ocean floor might be stopped from flowing normally, which can lead to environmental problems.","w":0.72049687703450527,"x":0.086112567425345593,"y":0.30194619964303193,"h":0.019450445090774982,"c":1},{"t":"Q34","x":0.80842911890937486,"y":0.30523255789864612,"w":0.04789271990458166,"h":0.011627907397322113,"c":1},{"y":0.35319767455685647,"w":0.70881225585937502,"h":0.01311079560580064,"t":"The second category of marine energy that I'll mention is tidal energy. One major advantage","x":0.090038316409591826,"c":1},{"y":0.36915297066806751,"w":0.6973180135091146,"c":1,"t":"of using the tide, rather than waves, as a source of energy is that it's predictable: we know","h":0.013114471049736731,"x":0.088122602312890028},{"y":0.38517441874056879,"c":1,"w":0.4291187540690104,"h":0.013081395068452073,"t":"the exact times of high and low tides for years to come.","x":0.088122615162424631},{"h":0.016401254121030551,"y":0.40791002617496419,"t":"For tidal energy to be effective, the difference between high and low tides needs to be at least","w":0.70699961344401041,"x":0.088069078863419081,"c":1},{"x":0.086146183833214041,"w":0.72425771077473955,"y":0.42303287946134094,"c":1,"h":0.017665795520343641,"t":"five metres, and this occurs naturally in only about forty places on Earth. But the right conditions"},{"c":1,"t":"can be created by constructing a tidal lagoon, an area of sea water separated from the sea.","w":0.68965515136718747,"x":0.088122615788782638,"h":0.013096095638540306,"y":0.44184576468432002},{"w":0.72222223917643236,"t":"One current plan is to create a tidal lagoon on the coast of Wales. This will be an area of water","x":0.08812259678454476,"y":0.46511627895554275,"h":0.014656160935740736,"c":1},{"h":0.013274336283185861,"t":"within a bay at Swansea, sheltered by a U-shaped breakwater, or dam, built out from the","c":1,"x":0.088122595787872765,"w":0.67624521891276035,"y":0.48103666235917053},{"y":0.49841972165862292,"x":0.086206898796704179,"h":0.014661673800230979,"t":"coast. The breakwater will contain sixteen hydro turbines, and as the tide rises, water rushes","c":1,"w":0.70881225585937502},{"y":0.51453488385786872,"h":0.013081395068451962,"x":0.088122595543208504,"t":"through the breakwater, activating the turbines, which turn a generator to produce electricity.","c":1,"w":0.70114944458007811},{"w":0.66870198567708328,"h":0.017514961257143691,"c":1,"y":0.52904237193718129,"t":"Then, for three hours as the tide goes out, the water is held back within the breakwater,","x":0.086153035159446459},{"c":1,"t":"increasing the difference in water level, until it's several metres higher within the lagoon than in","y":0.54505813978330986,"x":0.088122614559574305,"w":0.72222218831380214,"h":0.014676373767491091},{"h":0.013081395068451962,"x":0.088122600882710928,"t":"the open sea. Then, in order to release the stored water, gates in the breakwater are opened.","c":1,"y":0.56250000013842005,"w":0.71264368693033853},{"w":0.6840132141113282,"y":0.57667926566070338,"h":0.015998607640320683,"x":0.088064863623649792,"t":"It pours powerfully out of the lagoon, driving the turbines in the breakwater in the opposite","c":1},{"x":0.088122599713967797,"t":"direction and again generating thousands of megawatts of electricity. As there are two high","y":0.59447674407187356,"c":1,"w":0.69157089233398428,"h":0.014562447062033024},{"c":1,"y":0.61046511641737744,"t":"tides a day, this lagoon scheme would generate electricity four times a day, every day, for a","x":0.088122592986595971,"w":0.6954023234049479,"h":0.01311263302635457},{"c":1,"t":"total of around 14 hours in every 24 - and enough electricity for over 150,000 homes.","y":0.6264222500471518,"w":0.65708811442057291,"h":0.01611883691529703,"x":0.084291191728167597},{"c":1,"w":0.67241378784179684,"h":0.015988371616368346,"x":0.08620689907910152,"y":0.64970930256144921,"t":"This system has quite a lot in its favour: unlike solar and wind energy it doesn't depend"},{"h":0.014580821870401217,"c":1,"w":0.67049809773763014,"t":"on the weather; the turbines are operated without the need for fuel, so it doesn't create","x":0.086206889728391661,"y":0.66715116267619923},{"w":0.65144694010416671,"h":0.014686184194687812,"c":1,"y":0.68254000701884543,"t":"any greenhouse gas emissions; and very little maintenance is needed. It's estimated","x":0.08807471205423667},{"c":1,"t":"that electricity generated in this way will be relatively cheap, and that manufacturing the","w":0.67624521891276035,"h":0.016118836915297141,"y":0.69911504406291614,"x":0.086206892349096814},{"t":"components would create more than 2,000 jobs, a big boost to the local economy.","x":0.086206890016579746,"h":0.014656160935740625,"c":1,"y":0.7151162789533384,"w":0.63409962972005207},{"x":0.088122614328612764,"t":"On the other hand, there are fears that lagoons might harm both fish and birds, for example","h":0.014599197281597531,"c":1,"y":0.73982558128119269,"w":0.7049808247884114},{"y":0.75436046519472288,"x":0.086206895544293241,"t":"by disturbing migration patterns, and causing a build-up of silt, affecting local ecosystems.","c":1,"h":0.015988371616368346,"w":0.69731801350911449},{"t":"There are other forms of tidal energy, but I'll go on to the third category of marine energy:","y":0.77906976767747804,"w":0.68773946126302077,"x":0.086206897605063379,"h":0.01612618659751297,"c":1},{"x":0.088060350775511581,"c":1,"h":0.016575502836900236,"w":0.63038731892903654,"y":0.79364246169440233,"t":"ocean thermal energy conversion. This depends on there being a big difference in"},{"x":0.088078638223922395,"c":1,"y":0.80958048097625057,"h":0.016017669070083396,"w":0.70507975260416667,"t":"temperature between surface water and the water a couple of kilometres below the surface,"},{"x":0.088122603888264733,"y":0.82703488385740664,"w":0.68199234008789056,"h":0.013081395068451962,"c":1,"t":"and this occurs in tropical coastal areas. The idea is to bring cold water up to the surface"},{"w":0.51340998331705723,"t":"using a submerged pipe. The concept dates back to 1881, when ...","x":0.088122594448557828,"y":0.84292035376926377,"c":1,"h":0.013274336283185861},{"h":0.013081395068452073,"w":0.036398468017578289,"x":0.81992337126539672,"t":"Q35","y":0.36918604661094112,"c":1},{"y":0.48255813929039504,"c":1,"x":0.81992337125941006,"h":0.011627907397322113,"w":0.036398468017578178,"t":"Q36"},{"w":0.045977010726928724,"y":0.56250000010171797,"c":1,"t":"Q37","x":0.81034482790225582,"h":0.013081395068451962},{"c":1,"h":0.013081395068451962,"x":0.81992337126473147,"y":0.66715116289455301,"w":0.036398468017578067,"t":"Q38"},{"c":1,"w":0.036398468017578178,"y":0.709302325590774,"t":"Q39","x":0.81992337148929528,"h":0.013081395068451962},{"x":0.81992337126473147,"y":0.75581395324578349,"t":"Q40","h":0.011627907397322113,"c":1,"w":0.036398468017578067},{"x":0.86590038293635929,"y":0.95494186056442953,"t":"101","w":0.034482758839925132,"h":0.013081395068451962,"c":1}],"w":2400,"h":3164}